            <ArticleTitle>Atypical cause of radiculopathy - Intradural spinal arachnoid cyst.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>267-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/17843286.2016.1139288</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intradural spinal arachnoid cysts are a relatively uncommon lesion that may be either intra, or extradural, and intradural spinal arachnoid cysts are even less common. Arachnoid cysts are cerebrospinal fluid collections in the spine that can present with neurological symptoms. The objective of this paper is to describe a rare case of radicular pain due to a spinal arachnoid cyst.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
